  handler unit_conversion
    status "justified-native"
    primitive "rust/src/solver_handlers/unit_conversion.rs"
    justification "Exact decimal conversion arithmetic is a compiled primitive; the unit factors, conversion formulas, and response templates are seed data. Browser twin (PR #1188, JavaScript-first parity): js/worker/formal_ai_worker_units.js answers the same seed records in the worker."
  handler incompatible_units
    status migrated
    data "data/seed/meanings-units.lino|data/seed/multilingual-responses-synthesis.lino"
    primitive "rust/src/solver_handler_units.rs"
    justification "issue #918 (R914-6): the units, the dimensions they measure and their surfaces were already meaning-lexicon data; the last Rust and worker prose, the incompatibility sentence, is the seeded unit_incompatibility response with unit and dimension slots, English-only exactly as before. The native part is the language-neutral walk that finds two units the lexicon places in distinct dimensions. Browser twin: tryIncompatibleUnits in js/worker/formal_ai_worker_meaning_lexicon.js renders the same response; pinned in both runtimes (rust/tests/web/issue-0918-handler-rules-batch.test.mjs)."
    held_out "rust/tests/unit/issue_918_handler_rules_batch.rs"
  handler diagnostic
    status migrated
    surface prelude
    data "data/seed/handler-rules.lino"
    primitive "rust/src/meta_method_dispatch.rs"
    justification "issue #918 (R914-6): the per-message marker is the diagnostic_marker table of data/seed/handler-rules.lino, matched in the prompt and stripped from it in both runtimes, and it heads the appended evidence and trace block; the native part is the recursive solve of the unmarked prompt and the trace layout. Recognition used to test a literal in the lower-cased text while stripping it from the prompt, so an upper-case marker reached the inner solve unstripped and met itself again; the exact seeded marker now does both, a deliberate change, and a lower-case marker answers as before. The browser had no twin (a marked prompt answered unknown); tryDiagnosticMarker in js/worker/formal_ai_worker_native_lanes.js solves the unmarked prompt and appends the same evidence and trace lines under the marker, without the native links-notation lines, since the worker keeps no links projection of an answer. Pinned in both runtimes (rust/tests/web/issue-0918-handler-rules-batch-2.test.mjs)."
    held_out "rust/tests/unit/issue_918_handler_rules_batch_2.rs"
  handler nl_tool
    status migrated
    surface prelude
    data "data/seed/meanings-tool-access.lino|data/seed/multilingual-responses-synthesis.lino"
    primitive "rust/src/solver_handlers/natural_language_tools.rs"
    justification "issue #918 (R914-6): the calculator, web-search and local-shell tool calls are recognized through the seeded calculator_tool_name, web_search_tool_name, tool_invocation_cue, local_shell_request_cue and tool_argument_marker roles in both runtimes, and the seven report and refusal format strings of rust/src/solver_handlers/natural_language_tools.rs (and its requested-source frame) are seeded nl_tool_* responses; the native part is the agent-mode and package-permission gate, the bounded JavaScript subset and the calculator. English answers are byte-identical; the refusals now speak the prompt language in en, ru, hi, zh and es, a deliberate change (a Russian tool call used to be refused in English), while the tool reports stay English. The browser had no twin (a calculator tool call answered unknown, a web-search tool call ran the general search over the request words); tryNaturalLanguageToolRequest in js/worker/formal_ai_worker_nl_tools.js refuses outside agent mode with the native sentence, runs the browser calculator in agent mode with the native report, and answers the seeded nl_tool_browser_unavailable refusal in the prompt language for the web-search tool call and the local shell, which it has no executor for. JavaScript execution keeps the worker sandbox handler. Pinned in both runtimes (rust/tests/web/issue-0918-handler-rules-batch-2.test.mjs)."
    held_out "rust/tests/unit/issue_918_handler_rules_batch_2.rs"
  handler behavior_rules
    status migrated
    surface prelude
    data "data/seed/meanings-behavior-rules.lino|data/seed/prompt-patterns.lino|data/seed/multilingual-responses-behavior-rules.lino|data/seed/intent-routing.lino"
    primitive "rust/src/solver_handlers/behavior_rules.rs"
    justification "R1188-U1 (generalize, do not specialize): recognition is the seeded rule_listing_*, rule_count_*, rule_brief_request and, new, rule_detail_request roles and the behavior_rules_list prompt patterns in both runtimes (the detail openings were an inline prefix list in each); every topic heading, rule label, matched-prompt line, response description, When X then Y statement, list footer, change hint, count and brief sentence and taught-rule answer is a seeded behavior_rule_* response of data/seed/multilingual-responses-behavior-rules.lino in en, ru, hi, zh and es, filled in one pass. The handler keeps the eight-row catalog of ids, topics, intents and sources, the natural-language skill compiler that turns a dialog message into a rule, and its replay. The browser twin (js/worker/formal_ai_worker_behavior_rules_and_self_facts.js and _04.js) renders the same records and now answers byte-identically to the native pins in all four pinned languages, where it used to hold a drifted copy (another topic order, another write-program label and matches line, an English-only assistant-name statement). The example prompts the help shows are data, so no test prompt is held verbatim in code (data/meta/prompt-specialization-ratchet.lino at 0)."
    held_out "rust/tests/unit/specification/behavior_rules.rs"
  handler feature_capability
    status migrated
    surface prelude
    data "data/seed/feature-capabilities.lino|data/seed/multilingual-responses-capabilities.lino|data/seed/meanings-feature-capability.lino"
    primitive "rust/src/solver_handlers/feature_capability.rs"
    justification "issue #918 (R914-6): the prelude row recognizes a capability question through the feature_capability_question and feature_capability_alias roles, reads the features, their runtime switches and their localized labels and examples from data/seed/feature-capabilities.lino, and renders every yes, no, reason and web-search sentence from the seeded feature_capability_* responses; the handler keeps only the switch-to-runtime mapping. The two runtimes had hand-kept tables that drifted (the browser said diagnostics where the native row said diagnostic trace, and a dozen labels and examples differed); the seed holds the native table, a deliberate parity fix for the browser answers. Each runtime keeps its own web-search unavailable sentence, since the browser speaks of its session and the native row of its configuration."
    held_out "rust/tests/unit/specification/capabilities.rs"
